        "original_id": "ea0e57bd-44c8-5ef1-9f73-9f6e09534f34",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Arthur Russell, Jerry Harrison, Tony Bongiovi, Lance Quinn\n- Bands: Hecuba, Talking Heads\n- Works: Wild Combination, Psycho Killer\n- Places: Los Angeles\n\nFacts:\n- Arthur Russell was born Charles Arthur Russell Jr. on May 21, 1951, and he died on April 4, 1992.\n- Arthur Russell was an American cellist, composer, producer, singer, and musician whose work spanned many styles.\n- In 1992, Jerry Harrison wrote in the liner notes for a release that an acoustic b-side version of “Psycho Killer” featured Arthur Russell on cello.\n- In that 1992 note, Jerry Harrison said he was glad Tony Bongiovi and Lance Quinn were persuaded that the version with cellos should not be the only one.\n- Hecuba performed in Los Angeles at the premiere of “Wild Combination,” a film about Arthur Russell.\n- Hecuba performed their versions of Arthur Russell’s music at the Los Angeles premiere of “Wild Combination.”",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
